## NOTE — PARKED, NOT CLAIMABLE

**BLOCKED pending ADR-0015 sign-off — do NOT un-park (rename to `WCI.md`) until the WCI
reshape is finalized, ADR-0015 is written, and the operator signs off.**

This ticket is staged as `.parked` (off the active board) on purpose: its design is not yet
signed off. `depends_on: ADR-0015` is the genuine gate — the design must be SIGNED OFF before
WCI builds against it. **It is NOT gated on TIER7B:** the owns sets are disjoint (WCI owns
`engine/{reconcile,scheduler,board}.py`; TIER7B owns `router/api/adapters.acp/failover.py`), so
WCI-MVP can build **concurrently with TIER7B** once ADR-0015 is signed off. The earlier
`depends_on: TIER7B` was a mere ordering relation (the exact disjoint-owns ≠ build-dependency
mislabel the WCI reconciler is meant to catch) and has been dropped.

Design source: `DSGN-WCI-reshape.md`. Adversarial review blessed the MVP as **WCI-1 (static
reconciler — re-port/consolidate the existing redundancy/contradiction checks) + WCI-2 (depth
pre-sort of the ready set)** as clean and shippable. WCI-4 (`merge_after` edge type) is under a
separate reshape-fix; WCI-6 (auto-slice) is parked. Neither is in this ticket's scope.

Un-park checklist (all required before rename to `WCI.md`):
1. WCI reshape (`DSGN-WCI-reshape.md`) finalized.
2. ADR-0015 (work-composition intelligence: reconcile + ordering layer) written.
3. Operator sign-off.
4. Build prompt created at the `prompt:` path above (validate_board will go RED until it exists —
   intentional un-park tripwire).
